CORE dfcc-only broken-z3-smt-backend broken-cprover-smt-backend no-new-smt
main.c
--dfcc main --enforce-contract set_a _ --slice-formula --object-bits 16 --verbosity 9
^\d{1,6} variables, \d+ clauses$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^\d{7,} variables, \d+ clauses$
--
The check that `p->a` is assignable is discharged during symbolic execution, so
with --slice-formula nothing depends on the branch in
__CPROVER_contracts_write_set_check_assignment that looks `ptr` up in the set of
locally allocated objects, and the assignments that define that set are sliced
away. The condition of that branch must then not be converted: doing so creates
unconstrained variables for the whole set, which holds 2^object-bits pointers.
With 16 object bits the formula used to have more than 8 million variables.
